/* ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬ÂÃ¢â€šÂ¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬ÂÃ¢â€šÂ¬ Section rhythm ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬ÂÃ¢â€šÂ¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬ÂÃ¢â€šÂ¬ */
.cms-page{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--gap-section)}
.cms-page>*{margin-top:0;margin-bottom:0}
/* A block's own leading margin would fight the flex gap and produce the uneven
   runs between sections. The gap is the single source of vertical spacing. */
.cms-block{min-width:0}
.cms-stack{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--gap-block);min-width:0}

/* ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬ÂÃ¢â€šÂ¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬ÂÃ¢â€šÂ¬ Rows and columns ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬ÂÃ¢â€šÂ¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬ÂÃ¢â€šÂ¬ */
.cms-row{display:grid;gap:var(--gap-col);align-items:start;min-width:0}
.cms-row>.cms-col{min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:var(--gap-block)}
/* Equal height: columns stretch, the card inside fills, and a "+N more" link
   pins to the bottom so two columns end flush instead of one dangling short. */
.cms-row.eqh{align-items:stretch}
.cms-row.eqh>.cms-col{height:100%}
/* Three levels have to stretch, not one: the column, the block wrapper inside
   it, and the card inside that. Stretching only the card left it 60px short of
   its neighbour, because the wrapper between them was still shrink-to-fit. */
.cms-row.eqh>.cms-col>.cms-block{flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-height:0}
.cms-row.eqh>.cms-col>.cms-block>.ev-card,
.cms-row.eqh>.cms-col>.cms-block>.card,
.cms-row.eqh>.cms-col>.cms-block>.reel,
.cms-row.eqh>.cms-col>.cms-block>.split{flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column}
/* Recognition and the booth strip are cards too — they just wrap themselves in
   their own class, so they were missing from the list above and took an equal
   slot only to draw a short card inside it. No min-height:0 on these: the card
   must never be squeezed below the rows it holds, which is what would turn an
   overrun into content clipped by the rounded corner. */
.cms-row.eqh>.cms-col>.cms-block>.tqr,
.cms-row.eqh>.cms-col>.cms-block>.booth-reel-wrap{flex:1;display:flex;
  flex-direction:column}
/* Its own rule sets 250px for a column that stands on its own; in an
   equal-height row the row decides. */
.cms-row.eqh .booth-reel-wrap{height:auto}
/* The rows never share out the card's height. They used to — flex:1 each — and
   that is what made them different heights from one another, because five rows
   dividing an odd number of leftover pixels do not divide it evenly. The card is
   as tall as its rows and stops there, which is also where the section ends. */
.cms-row.eqh>.cms-col>.cms-block>.tqr{justify-content:flex-start;flex:none}
.cms-row.eqh>.cms-col>.cms-block>.tqr>.tqr-row{flex:none}

/* The project carousel in an equal-height row. Its slide is a fixed 330px,
   which is right on its own and wrong beside a taller card: the column would
   either stop short or, once the row stretched to match, gain a black gap
   under the picture. `1 0 330px` keeps 330 as the floor and lets the picture
   take whatever height the row settles on. */
.cms-row.eqh>.cms-col>.cms-block>.reel>.carousel{flex:1;display:flex;
  flex-direction:column;min-height:0}
.cms-row.eqh>.cms-col>.cms-block>.reel>.carousel>.slide{flex:1 0 330px}
@media(max-width:900px){
  .cms-row{grid-template-columns:1fr!important}
}

/* ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬ÂÃ¢â€šÂ¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬ÂÃ¢â€šÂ¬ Blocks promoted out of the homepage so they work on any page ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬ÂÃ¢â€šÂ¬ÃƒÂ¢Ã¢â‚¬ÂÃ¢â€šÂ¬ */
/* The greeting reads as a header rather than as the first paragraph of the page.
   It was type on the page background with a rule under it, which is a heading
   and not a masthead.
   Flat, and yellow on one edge only. The version before this washed the corner
   in yellow over a drafting grid, which is a great deal of decoration to put
   behind somebody's own name — and it fought the tile strip directly beneath
   it. A plain panel and a single bar hold the top of the page just as firmly
   and then get out of the way. */
/* The yellow runs along the top edge, and the corners are square. A one-sided
   accent only reads as deliberate on a square box: as a border-left on a 14px
   rounded card it terminated in a straight edge against a curve at both ends,
   which is what made it look stuck on rather than part of the panel. */
.home-top{display:block;padding:0;position:relative;
  background:var(--paper-2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-top:5px solid var(--yellow);
  border-radius:0;box-shadow:0 12px 32px -22px rgba(18,18,16,.4)}
.home-top::before{content:none}
.home-top::after{content:none}
.ht-main{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:flex-end;
  gap:var(--sp-6);flex-wrap:wrap;padding:24px 28px 22px}

/* The three things worth knowing. Without them the header announced the
   reader's own name and the current time, and stopped. */
.ht-strip{display:flex;border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:14px 28px 16px}
.hts{flex:1;min-width:0;padding-left:14px;border-left:1px solid var(--line)}
.hts:first-child{border-left:3px solid var(--yellow);padding-left:13px}
.hts-k{font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.09em;
  color:var(--muted);font-weight:700}
.hts-v{font-size:13.5px;font-weight:650;color:var(--ink);margin-top:4px;
  white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
.hts-v.muted-v{color:var(--muted);font-weight:600}
.hts-s{font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:2px;
  white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}

/* ── the birthdays hover card ── */
.hts-bd{position:relative}
.hts-bd.has-pop{cursor:default;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;transition:background .13s}
.hts-bd.has-pop:hover,.hts-bd.has-pop:focus-visible{background:var(--paper);outline:none}
.bd-pop{position:absolute;top:calc(100% + 12px);right:0;width:330px;z-index:90;
  background:var(--paper-2);border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:12px;padding:6px;
  box-shadow:0 22px 50px -18px rgba(18,18,16,.45),0 0 0 1px rgba(18,18,16,.04);
  opacity:0;visibility:hidden;transform:translateY(-5px);
  transition:opacity .14s,transform .14s,visibility .14s}
.hts-bd:hover .bd-pop,.hts-bd:focus-within .bd-pop{opacity:1;visibility:visible;transform:none}
/* Bridges the gap between the tile and the card, so crossing it with the
   pointer does not count as leaving. */
.bd-pop::before{content:"";position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:-14px;height:14px}
.bd-pop-h{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:baseline;gap:10px;
  padding:9px 10px 10px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);margin-bottom:4px}
.bd-pop-h b{font-size:13px;font-weight:650}
.bd-pop-h span{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)}
.bd-pop-list{max-height:296px;overflow:auto}
/* ══ files waiting to be uploaded ═══════════════════════════════════════════
   The pictures themselves instead of "9 photos selected". A count is a number
   you have to trust; the thumbnails are how you see that the right nine are
   there, and notice the wrong one.                                     ══════ */
.bm-pending{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;background:var(--paper);
  padding:12px;margin-bottom:12px}
.bm-pending-h{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:11px}
.bm-pending-h b{font-size:13px}
.bm-pending-h span{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);font-family:var(--mono,monospace)}
/* The two buttons sit together at the far end, away from the count. */
.bm-pending-h .btn:first-of-type{margin-left:auto}
.bm-pending-grid{display:grid;gap:10px;
  grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(112px,1fr))}
.bm-pend{position:relative;border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--paper-3);
  aspect-ratio:1;border:1px solid var(--line-2)}
.bm-pend img,.bm-pend video{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block}
/* The filename, over a gradient so it stays readable on a pale photo. */
.bm-pend-n{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;bottom:0;padding:14px 7px 5px;
  font-size:10.5px;line-height:1.3;color:#fff;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;
  white-space:nowrap;
  background:linear-gradient(to top,rgba(0,0,0,.82),rgba(0,0,0,0))}
.bm-pend-x{position:absolute;top:5px;right:5px;width:24px;height:24px;border:none;
  border-radius:50%;background:rgba(18,18,16,.72);color:#fff;font-size:16px;line-height:1;
  cursor:pointer;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:0;
  opacity:0;transition:opacity .12s,background .12s}
.bm-pend:hover .bm-pend-x,.bm-pend-x:focus-visible{opacity:1}
.bm-pend-x:hover{background:var(--bad)}
/* Touch has no hover, so the remove button is simply always there. */
@media (hover:none){.bm-pend-x{opacity:1}}
.bm-pend.vid::after{content:"VIDEO";position:absolute;top:6px;left:6px;
  font-size:9px;font-weight:800;letter-spacing:.08em;padding:2px 6px;border-radius:4px;
  background:var(--yellow);color:var(--on-yellow)}

/* ══ the meeting composer, opened from the calendar ═════════════════════════
   Light, unlike the room-booking dialog: this one is opened from a white page
   by anybody, not dragged out of a dark scheduling grid.               ══════ */
.cal-newmeeting{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:14px}
.cal-newmeeting .muted{font-size:12.5px}
.mc-back{position:fixed;inset:0;background:rgba(18,18,16,.5);z-index:1100;
  opacity:0;visibility:hidden;transition:opacity .16s}
.mc-back.on{opacity:1;visibility:visible}
.mc{position:fixed;top:50%;left:50%;transform:translate(-50%,-48%) scale(.98);
  width:min(560px,calc(100vw - 32px));max-height:calc(100vh - 48px);overflow-y:auto;
  background:var(--paper-2);border-radius:14px;z-index:1101;opacity:0;visibility:hidden;
  box-shadow:0 30px 80px rgba(18,18,16,.4);
  transition:opacity .16s, transform .16s cubic-bezier(.22,1,.36,1)}
.mc.on{opacity:1;visibility:visible;transform:translate(-50%,-50%) scale(1)}
.mc-head{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:12px;
  padding:18px 22px 14px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
.mc-head h3{margin:0;font-size:17px;font-weight:700}
.mc-x{background:none;border:none;cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted);display:flex;
  padding:5px;border-radius:8px}
.mc-x:hover{color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper)}
.mc-body{padding:18px 22px;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:14px}
.mc-f{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:6px;flex:1;min-width:0}
.mc-f.narrow{flex:0 0 132px}
.mc-f label{font-size:11px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.07em;text-transform:uppercase;
  color:var(--muted)}
.mc-f label em{font-style:normal;color:var(--ink);margin-left:4px;
  letter-spacing:0;text-transform:none;font-weight:700}
.mc-f small{font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.5}
.mc input[type=text],.mc input[type=date],.mc input[type=time],.mc input[type=url],
.mc select,.mc textarea{
  width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:9px;
  padding:10px 12px;font-family:inherit;font-size:13.5px;outline:none;background:var(--paper-2);
  color:var(--ink);resize:vertical}
.mc input:focus,.mc select:focus,.mc textarea:focus{border-color:var(--ink)}
.mc-row{display:flex;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.mc-where{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:12px;padding:14px;
  border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;background:var(--paper)}
.mc-chk{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;cursor:pointer}
.mc-chk input{width:16px;height:16px;accent-color:var(--yellow)}
.mc-chk span{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:7px}
/* Free or taken, said while the form is being filled rather than on save. */
.mc-avail{font-size:12px;font-weight:700;padding:6px 10px;border-radius:7px;
  background:var(--paper-3);color:var(--muted)}
.mc-avail.free{background:var(--ok-bg);color:var(--ok)}
.mc-avail.busy{background:var(--bad-bg);color:var(--bad)}
.mc-note{margin:0;font-size:11.5px;line-height:1.55;color:var(--muted)}
.mc-actions{display:flex;gap:10px;padding:14px 22px 18px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
.mc-actions .btn{flex:1;justify-content:center}
@media(max-width:520px){.mc-f.narrow{flex:1 1 100%}}

/* ── the birthday wish dialog, shared by the header strip and the block ── */
.bdw{position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:1200;background:rgba(18,18,16,.45);
  display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;padding:20px}
.bdw[hidden]{display:none}
.bdw-box{position:relative;background:var(--paper-2);width:100%;max-width:430px;
  padding:26px 24px 22px;border-radius:14px;box-shadow:0 24px 70px rgba(18,18,16,.3)}
.bdw-x{position:absolute;top:10px;right:12px;background:none;border:none;cursor:pointer;
  font-size:22px;line-height:1;color:var(--muted-2);padding:4px 8px;border-radius:8px}
.bdw-x:hover{color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper)}
.bdw-cake{font-size:26px;margin-bottom:6px}
.bdw-who{font-weight:700;font-size:17px}
.bdw-sub{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);margin:3px 0 16px}
.bdw-emoji{display:flex;gap:7px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:12px}
.bdw-e{width:36px;height:36px;background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);
  cursor:pointer;border-radius:9px;font-size:17px;line-height:1;transition:transform .1s}
.bdw-e:hover{transform:scale(1.15);border-color:var(--line-2)}
.bdw-msg{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:10px;
  padding:11px 13px;font-family:inherit;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.5;resize:vertical;outline:none}
.bdw-msg:focus{border-color:var(--ink)}
.bdw-presets{display:flex;gap:7px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin:10px 0 18px}
.bdw-p{background:var(--paper);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:20px;
  padding:6px 12px;font-size:11.5px;font-family:inherit;cursor:pointer;color:var(--ink-2)}
.bdw-p:hover{border-color:var(--ink);color:var(--ink)}
.bdw-act{display:flex;gap:9px}
.bdw-act .btn{flex:1;justify-content:center}
/* Already wished, so the row says so rather than offering to do it again. */
.bd-send.is-sent{opacity:.65;cursor:default}
.bd-row{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:7px 10px;border-radius:9px}
.bd-row:hover{background:var(--paper)}
.bd-av{width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:50%;flex:none;overflow:hidden;
  background:var(--disc);color:var(--yellow);display:flex;align-items:center;
  justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:11px}
.bd-av img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block}
.bd-who{min-width:0;flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;line-height:1.3}
.bd-who b{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:650;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;
  text-overflow:ellipsis}
.bd-who i{font-style:normal;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;
  overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
.bd-send{flex:none;border:1px solid var(--line-2);background:var(--yellow);
  color:var(--on-yellow);font-family:inherit;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;
  padding:6px 11px;border-radius:8px;cursor:pointer;
  transition:background .13s,border-color .13s,color .13s}
.bd-send:hover:not(:disabled){background:var(--yellow-2);border-color:var(--yellow-deep);color:var(--on-yellow)}
.bd-send:disabled{cursor:default;opacity:.85}
.bd-send.done{background:var(--ok-bg);border-color:var(--ok);color:var(--ok)}
.bd-nochat{flex:none;font-size:10.5px;color:var(--muted);cursor:help}

@media(max-width:820px){
  .ht-strip{flex-wrap:wrap;gap:12px}
  .hts{flex:1 1 46%}
  .bd-pop{right:auto;left:0;width:min(330px,calc(100vw - 40px))}
}
@media(max-width:640px){
  .ht-main{padding:20px 18px 16px}
  .ht-strip{padding:12px 18px 14px}
}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  .bd-pop{transition:none}
}
.ht-greet{font-size:19px;color:var(--muted);font-weight:500}
.ht-name{font-size:46px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:-.04em;line-height:.92;margin-top:var(--sp-1)}
.ht-clock{border:1px solid var(--line-2);padding:14px 18px;min-width:210px;background:var(--paper-2);display:flex;gap:26px}
.htc-k{font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.1em;color:var(--muted);font-weight:700}
.htc-v{font-family:'Draft B',sans-serif;font-size:23px;font-weight:700;margin-top:3px;letter-spacing:-.02em}
.htc-loc{margin-top:var(--sp-3);padding-top:var(--sp-3);border-top:1px solid var(--line);font-size:13px;
  color:var(--ink-2);font-weight:600;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:var(--sp-2)}
.htc-loc svg{color:var(--ink-2)}

.news-row{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:var(--sp-3);padding:10px 0;
  border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-decoration:none;color:inherit}
.news-row:last-of-type{border-bottom:none}
.news-row:hover .news-title{color:var(--ink)}
.news-pill{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:5px;padding:3px 9px;font-size:10.5px;
  font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;flex:none;height:fit-content}
.news-title{font-weight:700;font-size:14.5px;line-height:1.32;transition:color .13s}
.news-sub{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:6px}

/* The rows used to take `flex:1` and share out whatever height the card had
   spare, on the reasoning that a full card beats a short one in an equal-height
   row. It does not: beside a tall neighbour that stretched three articles 130px
   apart, and a list of three things spaced like that stops reading as a list.
   So they keep their own height and the card fills from the top. If the space
   under the last one bothers you, raise the block's limit — a fourth article
   fills it with something to read instead of with air.
   `min-height:0` because a flex child defaults to min-height:auto, which refuses
   to shrink below its content and would let a long summary push the card past
   its neighbour. */
.news-card .news-row{flex:0 0 auto;min-height:0;padding:12px 0}

/* The agenda fills its card the way the news card does. Three single-line
   entries in a 420px box left a third of it blank under the last one, which
   read as "nothing else today" when there was in fact more today — the "+N
   more" link was sitting in the middle of the gap saying so.
   `max-height` because flex:1 alone divides *all* the slack between however
   many rows there are, so a day with one meeting on it got one 270px-tall row.
   Rows grow to fill a normal day and stop before they look absurd on a quiet
   one. */
.cms-row.eqh>.cms-col>.cms-block>.split>.split-col{flex:1;display:flex;
  flex-direction:column;min-height:0}
/* Official events, filling the card rather than sitting in the top third of it.
   The stretch rule for this card was written against .home-row.eq, which is not
   a class the homepage puts on anything — the rows here are .cms-row.eqh — so
   the card kept its content height and left the rest of the frame empty.
   Each event then shares what is left, centred, with a ceiling so three events
   in a very tall column do not become three enormous bands. */
.cms-row.eqh>.cms-col>.cms-block>.ev-card{flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;min-height:0}
.cms-row.eqh>.cms-col>.cms-block>.ev-card>.ev{flex:1;min-height:0;max-height:104px;align-items:center}
.cms-row.eqh .split-col>.ag{flex:1;min-height:0;max-height:88px;padding:14px 0}
.cms-row.eqh .split-col>.ag .t{font-size:14px}
.cms-row.eqh .split-col>.ag .s{font-size:12.5px;margin-top:2px}
.news-excerpt{font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.5;color:var(--ink-2);margin-top:5px;
  display:-webkit-box;-webkit-line-clamp:2;-webkit-box-orient:vertical;overflow:hidden}

/* The article's picture, when it has one. Square and small on purpose: it is
   there to give the row something to look at, not to compete with the headline
   next to it. Rows without a picture simply run the full width — the alternative
   is a grey placeholder box, which is three squares pretending to be pictures. */
.news-thumb{flex:none;width:72px;height:72px;border-radius:10px;overflow:hidden;
  background:var(--paper-3);align-self:center}
.news-thumb img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block;
  transition:transform .35s var(--ease-out,cubic-bezier(.23,1,.32,1))}
.news-row:hover .news-thumb img{transform:scale(1.06)}

/* ══ AJi Booth strip ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   A row of album covers, scrolled sideways. The homepage is otherwise entirely
   bordered cards containing text, and a page built only of those reads as a
   list no matter how well each card is set — this is the one band on it that
   is a picture. Sideways rather than wrapped because a second row would make
   it a gallery, and the page has enough to read already.            ══════ */
/* The track still scrolls — that is what keeps a swipe working on a phone and
   what the arrows drive — but its scrollbar is gone. A browser scrollbar under
   a row of photographs is furniture, and "there is more this way" belongs on a
   control you can see and press. */
.booth-reel-wrap{position:relative}
.booth-reel{display:flex;gap:12px;overflow-x:auto;padding:2px 2px 4px;
  scroll-snap-type:x proximity;scrollbar-width:none;-ms-overflow-style:none;
  scroll-behavior:smooth}
.booth-reel::-webkit-scrollbar{display:none}

/* Over the pictures, not beside them: arrows in the margin would push the strip
   in from both edges and lose most of a tile to white space. Hidden outright at
   either end rather than dimmed — a greyed arrow still invites the press. */
.booth-nav{position:absolute;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);z-index:3;
  width:40px;height:40px;border:none;border-radius:99px;cursor:pointer;
  display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
  background:rgba(255,255,255,.94);color:#121210;
  box-shadow:0 6px 18px -6px rgba(18,18,16,.45),0 0 0 1px rgba(18,18,16,.07);
  transition:background 140ms,transform 140ms var(--ease-out,ease)}
.booth-nav:hover{background:var(--yellow);color:var(--on-yellow)}
.booth-nav:active{transform:translateY(-50%) scale(.94)}
.booth-nav[hidden]{display:none}
.booth-nav.l{left:-6px}
.booth-nav.r{right:-6px}
@media(max-width:640px){
  .booth-nav{display:none}   /* a thumb is a better control than a 40px target */
}
.booth-tile{position:relative;flex:none;width:232px;height:150px;overflow:hidden;
  border-radius:12px;background:var(--bed);scroll-snap-align:start;
  text-decoration:none;display:block;
  transition:transform .18s var(--ease-out,cubic-bezier(.23,1,.32,1)),
             box-shadow .18s}
.booth-tile img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block;
  transition:transform .5s var(--ease-out,cubic-bezier(.23,1,.32,1))}
.booth-tile:hover{transform:translateY(-3px);box-shadow:0 14px 30px -12px rgba(18,18,16,.5)}
.booth-tile:hover img{transform:scale(1.07)}
/* The caption sits on the photograph, so it needs its own contrast rather than
   the picture's — a white name on a pale sky is not a caption. */
.booth-tile-veil{position:absolute;inset:0;
  background:linear-gradient(to top,rgba(10,10,10,.82) 0%,rgba(10,10,10,.28) 42%,transparent 68%)}
.booth-tile-txt{position:absolute;left:13px;right:13px;bottom:11px;
  display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1px;color:#fff}
.booth-tile-txt b{font-size:13.5px;font-weight:700;line-height:1.25;
  overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;white-space:nowrap}
.booth-tile-txt i{font-style:normal;font-size:11px;color:rgba(255,255,255,.72)}
.booth-tile::after{content:"";position:absolute;inset:0;border-radius:12px;
  box-shadow:inset 0 0 0 1px rgba(255,255,255,.09)}
.booth-reel-empty{color:var(--muted);font-size:13px;padding:20px 0}
/* Beside a full-height carousel, a one-line message pinned to the top left of
   410px of nothing reads as a broken card rather than as an empty one. It fills
   what it was given and says plainly that there is nothing here yet. */
.cms-row.eqh .booth-reel-empty{flex:1;display:flex;align-items:center;
  justify-content:center;text-align:center;padding:20px;background:var(--paper);
  border:1px dashed var(--line-2);border-radius:12px}
@media(max-width:640px){
  .booth-tile{width:190px;height:126px}
}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  .booth-tile,.booth-tile img{transition:none}
  .booth-tile:hover{transform:none}
  .booth-tile:hover img{transform:none}
}

/* Where a Download button would be, on a document that may only be read. The
   gap on its own reads as a missing feature; this says it is a decision. */
/* ══ One library's settings page ════════════════════════════════════════════
   Its own page rather than a drawer in the management list. Who may read a
   library needs radio groups, a group list and a people search; none of that
   fits in a table row, and inside the dark bar it was rendering white on
   white.                                                            ══════ */
.ls-note{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;
  background:var(--warn-bg);border:1px solid var(--warn);border-radius:12px;
  padding:13px 16px;margin-bottom:18px;font-size:12.5px;line-height:1.6}
.ls-note svg{color:var(--warn);flex:none}
.ls-note span{flex:1;min-width:220px}

.ls-form{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:16px}
/* Squared, like every other panel on the Hub. These were rounded from before
   the corners were settled, which is visible the moment one sits next to a
   folder tile or a document row. */
.ls-card{background:var(--paper-2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:0;
  padding:20px 22px;margin-bottom:16px}
.ls-card h2{font-size:15.5px;margin:0 0 4px;letter-spacing:-.01em}
.ls-card.danger{border-color:var(--bad)}
.ls-card.danger h2{color:var(--bad)}
.ls-lede{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65;margin:0 0 14px;
  max-width:74ch}
.ls-n{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-width:22px;
  height:22px;padding:0 7px;margin-left:7px;border-radius:99px;
  background:var(--paper-3);color:var(--ink-2);font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;
  vertical-align:middle}

.ls-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(190px,1fr));gap:14px}
.ls-f{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;min-width:0}
.ls-f.wide{grid-column:span 2}
.ls-f.narrow{max-width:130px}
.ls-f>span{font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;
  color:var(--muted);font-weight:700;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px}
.ls-f em{font-style:normal;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:10px;
  font-weight:700;background:var(--yellow);color:var(--on-yellow);border-radius:20px;padding:1px 7px}
.ls-f input{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;border:1px solid var(--line-2);
  border-radius:8px;padding:9px 11px;font-family:inherit;font-size:13.5px;
  background:var(--paper-2);outline:none;transition:border-color .13s}
.ls-f input:focus{border-color:var(--ink)}

/* The form's footer, attached to the form. It was a pair of buttons left loose
   in the gap between two cards, then a full-width sticky bar that read as an
   empty panel with a button stranded in it. Neither looked like it belonged to
   anything. This is the card treatment with no top border, sitting flush under
   the last section, so the form and its confirm read as one object — and
   right-aligned, which is where a form's confirm goes. */
/* ══ A FORM'S FOOTER ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   One class for the row a form ends with. There were nineteen of them: eight
   named classes with different padding and different borders, and eleven written
   as inline styles because there was nothing to reach for — six of those eleven
   being the same declaration typed out six times.

   Left-aligned with the primary action first, which is what all nineteen already
   did. The convention was never the problem; having no shared place to put it
   was, so every new screen invented its own spacing and a few forgot the divider
   entirely. */
.f-foot{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;
  margin-top:20px;padding-top:16px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
/* The named footers, brought onto the same rules rather than rewritten in every
   template that uses them. Anything they set for themselves below still wins,
   which is how the ones sitting on a tinted ground keep it. */
.cx-actions,.ap-foot,.ma-form-foot,.tq-review-f,.ns-save,.nv-actions,
.gs-foot,.evm-actions,.hm-wa-acts{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;
  flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:20px;padding-top:16px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}

/* .it-bar had no rule at all — eight rows of buttons on the IT screens sitting
   shoulder to shoulder with no gap. It is a toolbar rather than a form's
   footer ("Back up now", "Restore"), so it gets the spacing and not the divider:
   a rule across the top of a toolbar says the thing above it has ended, and on
   these screens it has not. */
.it-bar{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:9px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:14px}

/* A compact editor's footer — a comment, a recognition — keeps its own tighter
   spacing and its right alignment. It sits inside a box the width of a text
   field, where a 20px gap and a full-width rule read as a page break. */
.cmt-edit-f{display:flex;justify-content:flex-end;align-items:center;gap:7px;
  margin-top:8px}

/* A form built as a stack of separate cards has no card to sit inside, so its
   footer is its own bar, flush under the last one. This was a pair of buttons
   loose in the gap between two cards, then a sticky bar that read as an empty
   panel with a button stranded in it. */
.f-foot.bar,.ls-actions{margin-top:-16px;padding:14px 18px;
  border:1px solid var(--line);border-top:none;background:var(--paper-2)}
/* The cards keep a margin-bottom from before this form was a flex column, so
   every gap in it was the flex gap *plus* that margin — 32px, and a footer
   pulled up by 16 still sat 16 clear of the card it belongs to. */
.ls-form>.ls-card{margin-bottom:0}
/* Inside a card — a single document's row — the card is the container already,
   so the footer is a plain row with no ground of its own. */
.ls-actions.right,.ls-doc-body .ls-actions{border:none;background:none;padding:0;
  margin:14px 0 0}
.ls-docs{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px}
.ls-doc{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:11px;overflow:hidden;background:var(--paper-2)}
.ls-doc[open]{border-color:var(--line-2)}
.ls-doc>summary{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;padding:11px 14px;
  cursor:pointer;list-style:none;transition:background .12s}
.ls-doc>summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
.ls-doc>summary:hover{background:var(--paper)}
.ls-doc-t{flex:1;min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;line-height:1.35}
.ls-doc-t b{font-size:13.5px;font-weight:650;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;
  text-overflow:ellipsis}
.ls-doc-t i{font-style:normal;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);
  white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
.ls-doc-state{flex:none;font-size:11px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink-2);
  background:var(--paper-3);border-radius:20px;padding:3px 10px;white-space:nowrap}
.ls-doc>summary svg{color:var(--muted);flex:none;transition:transform .18s}
.ls-doc[open]>summary svg{transform:rotate(180deg)}
.ls-doc-body{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:14px;background:var(--paper-2)}
/* Inside a document panel the access block is already on a card, so it does not
   need a second border around itself. */
.ls-doc-body .acc{margin-top:0;border:none;padding:0;background:none}

/* On the management list: a link to the settings, or a note saying whose the
   library is when it is not yours. */
.pm-cat-settings{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;flex:none;
  padding:6px 12px;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.28);border-radius:8px;
  color:#fff;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:600;text-decoration:none;
  background:rgba(255,255,255,.08);white-space:nowrap;transition:background .12s}
.pm-cat-settings:hover{background:rgba(255,255,255,.2)}
.pm-cat-settings b{font-weight:700;border-left:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.28);
  padding-left:8px;margin-left:2px}
.pm-cat-settings.ro{opacity:.6;cursor:help;background:none}

@media(max-width:720px){
  .ls-f.wide{grid-column:span 1}
}

/* ══ Access controls ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   Folded away on each library and document. Most are open to everybody, and
   the summary says which without anybody having to open it.        ══════ */
.acc-fold{flex:none}
.acc-fold>summary{list-style:none;cursor:pointer;display:inline-flex;
  align-items:center;gap:5px;padding:6px 11px;border:1px solid var(--line-2);
  border-radius:8px;font-size:11.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink-2);
  background:var(--paper-2);white-space:nowrap;transition:background .12s}
.acc-fold>summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
.acc-fold>summary:hover{background:var(--paper)}
.acc-fold[open]>summary{background:var(--paper-3);border-color:var(--ink)}

.acc{flex-basis:100%;margin-top:12px;padding:16px 18px;background:var(--paper-2);
  border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px}
.acc-modes{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:8px;margin-bottom:14px}
.acc-mode{display:flex;align-items:flex-start;gap:9px;cursor:pointer;
  padding:8px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:9px;
  transition:border-color .12s,background .12s}
.acc-mode:hover{background:var(--paper)}
.acc-mode:has(input:checked){border-color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper)}
.acc-mode input{margin-top:2px;accent-color:var(--yellow);flex:none}
.acc-mode b{display:block;font-size:13px;font-weight:650}
.acc-mode i{display:block;font-style:normal;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:1px}

/* Shown only once the choice above is "restricted": the lists mean nothing
   otherwise, and leaving them up invites somebody to fill them in and expect
   something to come of it. */
.acc-who{display:none;gap:18px;flex-wrap:wrap;padding-top:4px}
.acc.show-who .acc-who{display:flex}
.acc-block{flex:1;min-width:230px;margin-bottom:12px}
.acc-k{font-size:10px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.06em;
  color:var(--muted);font-weight:700;margin-bottom:7px}
.acc-groups{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px}
.acc-chk{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font-size:12.5px;
  padding:5px 10px;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;cursor:pointer;
  background:var(--paper-2)}
.acc-chk:has(input:checked){border-color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper-3)}
.acc-chk input{accent-color:var(--yellow)}
.acc-sel{border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:8px;padding:7px 10px;
  font-family:inherit;font-size:12.5px;background:var(--paper-2)}

.acc-people{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:6px;margin-bottom:8px}
.acc-chip{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;font-size:12px;
  background:var(--paper-3);border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:20px;
  padding:4px 6px 4px 11px}
.acc-chip button{border:none;background:none;cursor:pointer;font-size:15px;
  line-height:1;color:var(--muted);padding:0 3px}
.acc-chip button:hover{color:var(--bad)}
.acc-search{position:relative}
.acc-search input{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;border:1px solid var(--line-2);
  border-radius:8px;padding:8px 11px;font-family:inherit;font-size:12.5px;background:var(--paper-2)}
.acc-results{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:calc(100% + 4px);z-index:70;
  background:var(--paper-2);border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:10px;padding:4px;
  box-shadow:0 18px 40px -16px rgba(18,18,16,.4);max-height:230px;overflow:auto}
.acc-results[hidden]{display:none}
.acc-res{display:block;width:100%;text-align:left;border:none;background:none;
  cursor:pointer;padding:7px 9px;border-radius:7px;font-family:inherit;font-size:12.5px}
.acc-res:hover{background:var(--paper)}
.acc-res i{display:block;font-style:normal;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)}
.acc-dl{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding-top:12px;margin-bottom:0}
.acc-note{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6;margin-top:8px;
  max-width:60ch}

.pol-viewonly{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;padding:0 11px;height:31px;
  border:1px dashed var(--line-2);border-radius:8px;color:var(--muted);
  font-size:11.5px;font-weight:600;cursor:help;white-space:nowrap}

/* ══ Document viewer ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   Opens over the page like the booth lightbox. A PDF arrives as pictures of its
   pages rendered on the server, so this is the same component for a scan, a
   photograph and a fifty-page policy — and a view-only document has nothing in
   the browser to save.                                              ══════ */
.dv{position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:1400;display:none;flex-direction:column;
  background:rgba(10,10,8,.94)}
.dv.open{display:flex}
body.dv-lock-scroll{overflow:hidden}

.dv-bar{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:16px;
  padding:10px 14px;background:rgba(18,18,16,.96);
  border-bottom:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.1);flex-wrap:wrap}
.dv-id{min-width:0;display:flex;flex-direction:column;line-height:1.3}
.dv-id b{color:#fff;font-size:14px;font-weight:650;white-space:nowrap;
  overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis;max-width:46vw}
.dv-id i{font-style:normal;font-size:11.5px;color:rgba(255,255,255,.55)}
.dv-tools{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;flex:none}
.dv-btn{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
  min-width:32px;height:32px;padding:0 10px;border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.18);
  background:rgba(255,255,255,.06);color:#fff;font-family:inherit;font-size:13px;
  font-weight:600;border-radius:8px;cursor:pointer;text-decoration:none;
  transition:background .12s,border-color .12s,opacity .12s}
.dv-btn:hover:not(:disabled){background:rgba(255,255,255,.16)}
.dv-btn:disabled{opacity:.3;cursor:default}
.dv-btn.on{background:var(--yellow);border-color:var(--yellow);color:var(--on-yellow)}
.dv-save{background:var(--yellow);border-color:var(--yellow);color:var(--on-yellow)}
.dv-save:hover{background:var(--yellow-2);color:var(--on-yellow)}
.dv-close{font-size:20px;line-height:1}
.dv-pages{color:rgba(255,255,255,.75);font-size:12px;min-width:56px;
  text-align:center;font-variant-numeric:tabular-nums}
.dv-sep{width:1px;height:20px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.14);margin:0 4px}
/* Says why there is no Save, rather than leaving a gap where one usually is. */
.dv-lock{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;height:32px;padding:0 11px;
  border:1px dashed rgba(255,255,255,.28);border-radius:8px;
  color:rgba(255,255,255,.66);font-size:11.5px;font-weight:600;cursor:help}

.dv-stage{flex:1;overflow:auto;padding:22px;display:flex;justify-content:center;
  align-items:flex-start}
.dv-stage img{width:100%;max-width:1100px;height:auto;display:block;
  background:var(--paper-2);box-shadow:0 24px 70px rgba(0,0,0,.55)}
.dv-load{color:rgba(255,255,255,.7);font-size:13.5px;padding:60px 20px;
  text-align:center;align-self:center}
.dv-err{color:#ffb4a2}

@media(max-width:720px){
  .dv-bar{padding:8px 10px}
  .dv-id b{max-width:100%}
  .dv-stage{padding:10px}
}

/* ══ Birthday burst ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   Confetti inside the chat window a birthday wish arrives in. Clipped to the
   pane on purpose — the celebration belongs to that conversation, not to the
   whole screen, and a shower of paper over the rest of the Hub would be
   something to switch off rather than something to enjoy.        ══════ */
.ch-burst{position:absolute;inset:0;overflow:hidden;pointer-events:none;z-index:40}
.ch-burst i{position:absolute;top:-6%;width:9px;height:9px;opacity:0;
  animation-name:chBurst;animation-timing-function:cubic-bezier(.22,.6,.35,1);
  animation-fill-mode:forwards}
@keyframes chBurst{
  0%{opacity:0;top:-6%;transform:translateX(0) rotate(0deg)}
  10%{opacity:1}
  100%{opacity:0;top:106%;transform:translateX(var(--dx)) rotate(var(--rot))}
}
/* The JS checks this too, so nothing is created; the rule is here in case a
   layer is already on screen when the setting changes. */
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  .ch-burst{display:none}
}

/* ══ Projects: editing ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
   One project used to be one row — nine controls on a single line that scrolled
   sideways, every field three characters wide, and the description the narrowest
   box of all. Each project is a panel now, closed until you open it, with the
   fields laid out on a grid that gives the long ones room.          ══════ */
.pjx-bulk{display:flex;gap:20px;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;
  flex-wrap:wrap;background:var(--paper-2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:5px solid var(--yellow);
  border-radius:14px;padding:18px 22px}
.pjx-bulk-txt{min-width:0;flex:1}
.pjx-bulk-txt b{display:block;font-size:14.5px;margin-bottom:3px}
.pjx-bulk-txt span{font-size:12.5px;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.6}
.pjx-bulk-act{display:flex;gap:9px;flex-wrap:wrap;flex:none}

/* Search on the manage screen. 379 edit forms is 1.5 MB of HTML and a page
   nobody can find anything in; the box is how you reach a project now. */
.pjx-find{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:14px}
.pjx-find-box{position:relative;flex:1;min-width:240px}
.pjx-find-box svg{position:absolute;left:12px;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);
  color:var(--muted);pointer-events:none}
.pjx-find-box input{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;border:1px solid var(--line-2);
  border-radius:9px;padding:10px 13px 10px 36px;font-family:inherit;font-size:13.5px;
  background:var(--paper-2);outline:none;transition:border-color .13s}
.pjx-find-box input:focus{border-color:var(--ink)}
.pjx-find-note{font-size:12px;flex-basis:100%}
/* Room for the clear button at the right-hand end of the box. */
.pjx-find-box input{padding-right:34px}
.pjx-find-x{position:absolute;right:8px;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);
  border:none;background:none;cursor:pointer;color:var(--muted-2);display:flex;
  padding:4px;border-radius:50%}
.pjx-find-x:hover{color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper-3)}
/* Searching. A quiet turning mark beside the box rather than a bar across the
   results, which would move the list on every keystroke. */
.pjx-find-spin{width:15px;height:15px;flex:none;border-radius:50%;
  border:2px solid var(--line-2);border-top-color:var(--ink);
  animation:pjxSpin .6s linear infinite}
@keyframes pjxSpin{to{transform:rotate(360deg)}}
/* The results heading sits with its count on one line and the note under it. */
.pjx-results .sec-head{margin-top:0;flex-wrap:wrap}

.pjx-check{flex-direction:row;align-items:flex-start;gap:9px;flex-wrap:wrap}
.pjx-check input{margin-top:2px;accent-color:var(--yellow);flex:none}
.pjx-check span{font-size:13px;font-weight:650;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;color:var(--ink)}
.pjx-check i{flex-basis:100%;font-style:normal;font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);
  padding-left:23px}

.pjx-list{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:9px}
.pjx-item{background:var(--paper-2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;overflow:hidden}
.pjx-item[open]{border-color:var(--line-2);box-shadow:0 14px 30px -22px rgba(18,18,16,.5)}
.pjx-item>summary{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:14px;padding:11px 15px;cursor:pointer;
  list-style:none;transition:background .12s}
.pjx-item>summary::-webkit-details-marker{display:none}
.pjx-item>summary:hover{background:var(--paper)}
.pjx-thumb{width:54px;height:40px;border-radius:8px;overflow:hidden;flex:none;
  background:var(--paper-3);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}
.pjx-thumb img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block}
.pjx-thumb i{font-style:normal;font-size:9px;color:var(--muted);text-align:center;line-height:1.2}
.pjx-sum{min-width:0;flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1px}
.pjx-sum b{font-size:14px;font-weight:650;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
.pjx-sum i{font-style:normal;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;
  overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
.pjx-tags{display:flex;gap:6px;flex-wrap:wrap;flex:none}
.pjx-chev{width:16px;height:16px;color:var(--muted);flex:none;transition:transform .18s}
.pjx-item[open] .pjx-chev{transform:rotate(180deg)}
.pjx-body{border-top:1px solid var(--line);padding:18px 15px 15px;background:var(--paper-2)}

.pjx-card.add{background:var(--paper-2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:18px}
.pjx-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(210px,1fr));gap:14px}
.pjx-f{display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:5px;min-width:0}
.pjx-f.wide{grid-column:span 2}
.pjx-f.full{grid-column:1/-1}
.pjx-f.narrow{max-width:150px}
.pjx-f>span{font-size:11px;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em;
  color:var(--muted);font-weight:700;display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px}
/* The two that are required say so where you are typing, not after you submit. */
.pjx-f em{font-style:normal;text-transform:none;letter-spacing:0;font-size:10px;
  font-weight:700;background:var(--yellow);color:var(--on-yellow);border-radius:20px;padding:1px 7px}
.pjx-f input,.pjx-f select,.pjx-f textarea{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;
  border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:8px;padding:9px 11px;font-family:inherit;
  font-size:13.5px;background:var(--paper-2);outline:none;transition:border-color .13s}
.pjx-f input:focus,.pjx-f select:focus,.pjx-f textarea:focus{border-color:var(--ink)}
.pjx-f textarea{resize:vertical;line-height:1.55;min-height:84px}
.pjx-f input:invalid:not(:placeholder-shown){border-color:var(--bad)}
.pjx-file i{font-style:normal;font-size:11px;color:var(--muted)}
.pjx-foot{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:flex-end;gap:12px;margin-top:16px}
.pjx-foot .muted{margin-right:auto}
.pjx-del{margin-top:12px;padding-top:12px;border-top:1px solid var(--line);text-align:right}
.pjx-none{background:var(--paper-2);border:1px dashed var(--line-2);border-radius:12px;padding:34px;
  text-align:center;color:var(--muted);font-size:13px}

/* ── the upload preview ── */
.pjx-tally{display:flex;gap:10px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:16px}
.pjx-t{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:10px;padding:9px 15px;font-size:12.5px;
  color:var(--ink-2);background:var(--paper-2)}
.pjx-t b{font-size:16px;margin-right:5px}
.pjx-t.add b{color:var(--ok)}
.pjx-t.upd b{color:var(--info)}
.pjx-t.err b{color:var(--bad)}
.pjx-errs{background:var(--bad-bg);border:1px solid var(--bad);border-radius:12px;
  padding:15px 18px;margin-bottom:16px;font-size:12.5px}
.pjx-errs b{display:block;margin-bottom:7px}
.pjx-errs ul{margin:0 0 8px;padding-left:19px;line-height:1.7}
.pjx-prev{background:var(--paper-2);border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;overflow-x:auto}
.pjx-prev table{width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;font-size:12.5px;min-width:720px}
.pjx-prev th{text-align:left;padding:10px 13px;font-size:10.5px;text-transform:uppercase;
  letter-spacing:.05em;color:var(--muted);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);white-space:nowrap}
.pjx-prev td{padding:10px 13px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);vertical-align:top}
.pjx-prev tr:last-child td{border-bottom:none}
.pjx-confirm{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:12px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:18px}

/* ══ Organisational hierarchy ═══════════════════════════════════════════════
   A drill-down, not a diagram. Everything here is one level: where you are, the
   trail back to the top, and what is directly underneath.            ══════ */
.org2-search{position:relative;max-width:440px;margin-bottom:18px}
.org2-search>svg{position:absolute;left:13px;top:50%;transform:translateY(-50%);
  width:16px;height:16px;color:var(--muted);pointer-events:none}
.org2-search input{width:100%;box-sizing:border-box;border:1px solid var(--line-2);
  border-radius:10px;padding:11px 14px 11px 38px;font-family:inherit;font-size:13.5px;
  background:var(--paper-2);outline:none;transition:border-color .13s}
.org2-search input:focus{border-color:var(--ink)}
.org2-results{position:absolute;left:0;right:0;top:calc(100% + 6px);z-index:60;
  background:var(--paper-2);border:1px solid var(--line-2);border-radius:12px;padding:5px;
  box-shadow:0 22px 50px -18px rgba(18,18,16,.4);max-height:340px;overflow:auto}
.org2-results[hidden]{display:none}
.org2-res{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;padding:8px 9px;border-radius:9px;
  text-decoration:none;color:inherit}
.org2-res:hover{background:var(--paper)}
.org2-res b{display:block;font-size:13px;font-weight:650}
.org2-res i,.org2-res u{display:block;font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;
  font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted)}
.org2-nores{padding:14px;text-align:center;color:var(--muted);font-size:12.5px}

.org2-crumbs{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:4px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-bottom:14px}
.org2-crumb{font-size:12.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--muted);text-decoration:none;
  padding:4px 8px;border-radius:7px;transition:background .12s,color .12s}
.org2-crumb:hover{background:var(--paper-3);color:var(--ink)}
.org2-crumb.on{color:var(--ink);background:var(--paper-3)}
.org2-sep{width:12px;height:12px;color:var(--line-2);flex:none}

.org2-focus{display:flex;gap:18px;align-items:flex-start;background:var(--paper-2);
  border:1px solid var(--line);border-left:5px solid var(--yellow);border-radius:14px;
  padding:20px 22px}
/* The board and the CEO are the two fixed points of the chart, so they are the
   two that do not look like everybody else. */
.org2-focus.kind-board{border-left-color:var(--ink)}
.org2-focus.kind-entity{border-left-color:var(--ink-3)}
.org2-focus-id{min-width:0;flex:1}
.org2-focus-id h2{font-size:23px;letter-spacing:-.02em;margin:0 0 3px}
.org2-role{font-size:13.5px;font-weight:600;color:var(--ink-2)}
.org2-meta{display:flex;gap:14px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:7px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}
.org2-note{border:1px dashed var(--line-2);border-radius:20px;padding:1px 9px;cursor:help}
.org2-actions{display:flex;gap:8px;flex-wrap:wrap;margin-top:14px}

.org2-av{width:44px;height:44px;border-radius:50%;flex:none;overflow:hidden;
  background:var(--disc);color:var(--yellow);display:flex;align-items:center;
  justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:14px;letter-spacing:.02em}
.org2-av.lg{width:66px;height:66px;font-size:19px}
.org2-av.sm{width:32px;height:32px;font-size:11px}
.org2-av img{width:100%;height:100%;object-fit:cover;display:block}

.org2-n{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-width:22px;
  height:22px;padding:0 7px;margin-left:8px;border-radius:99px;background:var(--paper-3);
  color:var(--ink-2);font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;vertical-align:middle}

.org2-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fill,minmax(292px,1fr));gap:12px}
.org2-card{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:13px;background:var(--paper-2);
  border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:12px;padding:13px 15px;
  text-decoration:none;color:inherit;
  transition:border-color .14s,transform .14s var(--ease-out,ease),box-shadow .14s}
.org2-card:hover{border-color:var(--line-2);transform:translateY(-2px);
  box-shadow:0 12px 26px -18px rgba(18,18,16,.5)}
/* A company reads as a place, a person as a face. */
.org2-card.kind-entity .org2-av{background:var(--yellow);color:var(--on-yellow);border-radius:11px}
.org2-card.kind-ceo .org2-av{border-radius:11px}
.org2-card-id{min-width:0;flex:1;display:flex;flex-direction:column;gap:1px}
.org2-card-id b{font-size:13.5px;font-weight:650;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;
  text-overflow:ellipsis}
.org2-card-id i,.org2-card-id u{font-style:normal;text-decoration:none;font-size:11.5px;
  color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
/* The number is how many people are underneath, which is the one thing that
   tells you whether going in is worth it. */
.org2-count{flex:none;min-width:30px;height:24px;padding:0 8px;border-radius:99px;
  background:var(--paper-3);color:var(--ink-2);font-size:11.5px;font-weight:700;
  display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center}
.org2-go{width:15px;height:15px;color:var(--line-2);flex:none}
.org2-empty{grid-column:1/-1;padding:34px;text-align:center;color:var(--muted);
  font-size:13px;background:var(--paper-2);border:1px dashed var(--line-2);border-radius:12px}

@media(max-width:640px){
  .org2-focus{flex-direction:column;gap:12px}
  .org2-focus-id h2{font-size:19px}
}
@media(prefers-reduced-motion:reduce){
  .org2-card{transition:none}
  .org2-card:hover{transform:none}
}

/* "Show more" under a paged list — the directory and AJi Skills. Centred and
   quiet: it is the end of what has loaded, not a call to action, and the count
   beside it is what tells you whether pressing again is worth it. */
.dir-more{display:flex;flex-direction:column;align-items:center;gap:8px;
  padding:26px 0 8px}
.dir-more[hidden]{display:none}
.dir-more .btn{min-width:190px;justify-content:center}
.dir-more .muted{font-size:12px}

/* Marks the agenda as coming from Outlook rather than the Hub's own calendar.
   Quiet on purpose: it is a provenance note, not a feature to advertise. */
.ag-src{font-size:9.5px;font-weight:700;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;
  padding:2px 6px;background:var(--paper-3);color:var(--muted);border:1px solid var(--line)}

.split-head{display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:space-between;gap:var(--sp-3);margin-bottom:14px}
.split-head-title{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;font-weight:700;font-size:14px}
.split-head-link{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:5px;font-size:12px;font-weight:700;
  padding:5px 11px;border:1px solid var(--line-2);transition:background .13s,border-color .13s;
  text-decoration:none;color:inherit}
.split-head-link:hover{background:var(--yellow);border-color:var(--yellow);color:var(--on-yellow)}
.ag-b{border-left:3px solid var(--line-2);padding-left:var(--sp-3)}
.ag.y .ag-b{border-left-color:var(--yellow)}
.ag-b .t{font-weight:700;font-size:13.5px}
.ag-b .s{color:var(--muted);font-size:12px}

/* Done, and staying on the card. Struck through and muted so it stops competing
   with what is still to come, but still there — the day reads better with this
   morning's meetings crossed off than with the card pretending they were never
   on it. The rail goes back to a hairline, because the yellow one means "next". */
.ag.done .ag-t{color:var(--muted);text-decoration:line-through}
.ag.done .ag-b{border-left-color:var(--line)}
.ag.done .ag-b .t{color:var(--muted)}
.ag.done .ag-b .t>span{text-decoration:line-through}
.ag.done .ag-b .s{color:var(--muted-2)}
/* The tick is what says finished. Struck-through text on its own reads as
   cancelled, which is the opposite of what happened. */
.ag-tick{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
  width:15px;height:15px;border-radius:50%;flex:none;margin-right:5px;
  background:var(--ok-bg);color:var(--ok);vertical-align:-2px}
.ag-clear{padding:11px 0 2px;font-size:12px;color:var(--muted)}

.slide-tags{position:absolute;top:18px;left:18px;z-index:2;display:flex;gap:var(--sp-2)}
.slide-tags .stag{background:var(--yellow);color:var(--on-yellow);font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;
  text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.07em;padding:5px 10px}
.slide-tags .divchip{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper-2);border:1px solid rgba(255,255,255,.28);
  font-size:10.5px;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.05em;padding:var(--sp-1) 9px}
.slide-status{position:absolute;top:18px;right:18px;z-index:2}
.slide-wm{position:absolute;right:18px;bottom:12px;z-index:1;font-weight:700;font-size:78px;
  letter-spacing:-.05em;color:rgba(255,255,255,.06);line-height:.8;pointer-events:none}
.cdots{position:absolute;bottom:16px;right:18px;z-index:3;display:flex;gap:var(--sp-2)}
.cdots span{width:8px;height:8px;background:rgba(255,255,255,.4);cursor:pointer;transition:.2s}
.cdots span.on{background:var(--yellow);width:22px;color:var(--on-yellow)}
.proj-slide{background-size:cover;background-position:center}
.carousel .arr{cursor:pointer;border:none;font-size:20px}

.bd-today{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(230px,1fr))}
.bd-card{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:13px;padding:var(--sp-1) var(--sp-5);border-left:1px solid var(--line)}
.bd-card:first-child{padding-left:var(--sp-1);border-left:none}
.bd-av{width:46px;height:46px;border-radius:50%;background:linear-gradient(135deg,var(--ink),#333);
  color:var(--yellow);display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;font-weight:700;font-size:15px;flex:none}
.bd-info{flex:1;min-width:0}
.bd-name{font-weight:700;font-size:14px;line-height:1.2;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
.bd-role{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:2px;white-space:nowrap;overflow:hidden;text-overflow:ellipsis}
.bd-wish{width:34px;height:34px;border-radius:50%;display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
  background:var(--yellow);border:none;cursor:pointer;flex:none;font-size:15px;transition:transform .14s;
  box-shadow:0 1px 4px rgba(18,18,16,.12);color:var(--on-yellow)}
.bd-wish:hover{transform:scale(1.12) rotate(-6deg)}

.com-chips{display:flex;gap:var(--sp-2);flex-wrap:wrap;padding-bottom:14px;
  border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);margin-bottom:2px}
.com-chip{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:7px;border:1px solid var(--line-2);
  background:var(--paper-2);padding:var(--sp-2) 13px;font-weight:600;font-size:13px;
  transition:background .13s,border-color .13s;text-decoration:none;color:inherit}
.com-chip:hover{background:var(--yellow);border-color:var(--yellow);color:var(--on-yellow)}
.com-chip .cnt{color:var(--muted);font-weight:600}
.thread-row{display:flex;gap:var(--sp-3);align-items:flex-start;padding:var(--sp-3) 0;
  border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);text-decoration:none;color:inherit}
.thread-row:last-of-type{border-bottom:none}
.thread-row:hover .thread-title{color:var(--ink)}
.thread-title{font-weight:700;font-size:13.5px;line-height:1.3;transition:color .13s}
.thread-meta{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);margin-top:2px}
.thread-stats{font-size:11.5px;color:var(--muted);white-space:nowrap;margin-left:auto;flex:none}

/* What kind of thread this is, as a mark rather than a word. "QUESTION" was
   102px wide to say what a speech bubble says in 26, and every title on the card
   started that far in. Square-ish rather than round so it reads as a tag and not
   as an avatar. */
.thread-ic{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;
  width:26px;height:26px;flex:none;border-radius:8px;margin-top:1px;
  background:var(--paper-3);color:var(--ink-2)}
.thread-ic.q{background:var(--yellow);color:var(--on-yellow)}
.thread-row:hover .thread-ic{background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper-2)}
.thread-row:hover .thread-ic.q{background:var(--yellow);color:var(--on-yellow)}

.pill-ok{background:var(--ok-bg);color:var(--ok)}
.pill-warn{background:var(--warn-bg);color:var(--warn)}
.pill-info{background:var(--info-bg);color:var(--info)}
.pill-mut{background:var(--paper-3);color:var(--muted)}

/* Components that set their own trailing margin double up with the flex gap
   inside the builder, which is where the uneven section spacing came from. */
.cms-page .sec-head{margin-top:0;margin-bottom:15px}
.cms-page .home-top,.cms-page .ql,.cms-page .split,.cms-page .home-row{margin-bottom:0}

@media(max-width:900px){
  .ql{grid-template-columns:repeat(3,1fr)}
  .ht-name{font-size:34px}
  .ht-clock{min-width:auto}
}
@media(max-width:540px){
  .ql{grid-template-columns:repeat(2,1fr)}
  .bd-today{grid-template-columns:1fr}
  .bd-card{border-left:none;padding-left:0;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}
  .bd-card:first-child{border-top:none}
}

