   The flex row stretched the figure to the height of the letter, so a 200x267
   portrait sat in a 200x542 box with 275px of dead space under it. The row now
   aligns to the top, the portrait has a deliberate 4:5 ratio, and the letter is
   held to a readable measure instead of running the full card width. */
.ceo-body{align-items:flex-start}
.ceo-fig{width:224px;align-self:flex-start}
.ceo-fig img,.ceo-fig>div{width:100%;aspect-ratio:4/5;object-fit:cover;display:block}
.ceo-letter{max-width:68ch}
@media(max-width:900px){
  .ceo-fig{width:180px}
}
@media(max-width:540px){
  .ceo-fig{width:100%;max-width:260px}
}

